service_account.json
credentials.json
client_secret_*.json
token.json
.streamlit/secrets.toml
# Nothing under data/ belongs in the repo. It holds things the app WRITES
# (settings, snapshots) and build artefacts it does not read at all — the
# three .xlsx sheet templates are generated by tools/make_templates.py and
# then uploaded to Drive, which is where the team's data lives. If the app
# does not read a file at runtime, it should not ship with the code
# (Hamid, 19 Aug 2026). utils/settings.py creates the folder when it first
# needs it, so a fresh clone is fine without it.
data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Documentation stays local (Hamid, 19 Aug 2026). SCHEMA / WORKFLOW /
# DECISIONS / TODO / SETUP / setup_server carry sheet ids, colleague names
# and the order history behind the design, and the repo exists to deploy the
# app rather than to carry the project's paperwork. Nothing in the app reads
# a .md file, so leaving them out changes nothing at runtime.
#
# Note this also catches a README — add one with `git add -f README.md` if
# the repo ever needs a front page.
*.md

# --- public branch only -----------------------------------------------------
# tools/ are one-off setup and build scripts. The app never imports them, and
# their sample rows carry real vendor names, quote references, tracking
# numbers and prices. Nothing is lost by leaving them out of a public repo —
# they still live on `main` and in the private one.
tools/

